# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files — real secrets never tracked, the template always is.
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Deploy console contract — host-side only, never tracked.
cicd/
/data/

# Infrastructure notes — NOT for a public repo.
# Hosting.md and cicd.md contain Cloudflare tunnel UUIDs, internal hostnames and
# host filesystem paths for the deploy machine. Poster.pdf is 11 MB of a
# competitor's marketing material.
# If this repo is private and you want them tracked, delete these three lines.
docs/Hosting.md
docs/cicd.md
docs/Poster.pdf

# The business plan. Marked "Internal" on every page: pricing, salaries,
# capital, revenue projections, and a named client's work order with its
# contract value. This repo is PUBLIC — it must never be tracked.
docs/f2.pdf

# Editor scratch files. `.gitignore`'s `.env*` does NOT cover these: nano and
# vim name their swap for `.env` as `..env.swp`, which starts with `..env`, so
# the pattern misses it and `git add -A` would commit a buffer of the secrets
# file to a public repo.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.*.sw[a-p]

# A clone of this repo made inside itself (easy to do when following
# DEPLOYMENT.md Step 2 on the wrong machine). Nested repos get committed as a
# gitlink, which is never what anyone wants.
/vkon.in/

# Exported DNS zone files. They carry the Cloudflare tunnel UUID and the full
# record set — infrastructure detail that has no business in a public repo.
*.txt
!requirements.txt

# Source logo artwork. The processed transparent PNGs in public/brand ship.
vkon_logo.jpeg

# Source PNGs for the hero backgrounds. Kept locally so the images can be
# re-exported, but ~6.5 MB each — the committed asset is the JPEG beside them.
public/segments/*.png

# Same for the category artwork: the delivered files are PNG-named JPEGs (plus
# one real PNG), kept locally for re-export. The committed asset is the .jpg.
public/categories/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch files from verification runs and IDE sessions.
#
# Added 2026-09-10. The repo had accumulated ~90 of these — 47 `verify-*.mjs`,
# a dozen `diag*`/`repro*`/`measure*`, and four `.temp_*`/`temp*` files that
# had actually been COMMITTED. The verification harness is deliberately not in
# the repo (HANDOFF.md §5: "rebuild them from this section if you need them"),
# so anything matching these belongs in a scratch directory, not here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
verify-*.mjs
test-*.mjs
diag*.mjs
repro*.mjs
measure*.mjs
final-check.mjs
.scratch-*
.temp_*
temp[0-9]*.png

# Recovery/handoff packages. `vkon-project-package.zip` was 31 MB and its
# extracted twin another 32 MB; neither belongs in git.
vkon-project-package/
vkon-project-package.*
*.zip

# A stray nested copy of the project appeared at ./vkon.in during the
# 2026-09-10 recovery — the same hazard the "nested repos" note below warns
# about, so it is named explicitly.
/vkon.in/

# Stock artwork as delivered. Each of these folders is an EPS plus a
# multi-megabyte JPEG — 19 MB and 14 MB respectively — and this repo is PUBLIC,
# so `git add -A` would push 33 MB of licensed source art to GitHub. They stay
# local so a background can be re-exported at a different size; what ships is
# the resized JPEG in `public/` beside the other backgrounds.
#
# Put any future stock download in `art-source/` and it is ignored automatically.
abstract-round-particles-dark-background-with-mesh-structures/
point-wave-diagonal-texture-abstract-dot-background-technological-cyberspace-background/
art-source/

# The same, for stock art that arrives as a loose file rather than a folder.
artistic-background-wallpaper-with-color-halftone-effect.jpg
